{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-80312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2}{|x+1|\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-80312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x+1|\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x+1|\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+1).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x+1|\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x+1|\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+1)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-80312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-80312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-80312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+1}{2})+C"] ["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+1)+C"] ["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-80312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{(6x+1)}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-(6x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4(1-(6x+1)^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x+1)^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((6x+1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{6x+1}{2}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{6x+1}{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-(6x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((6x+1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-114918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{4})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{6x+1}{2})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-114923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(2(x-3))+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-3}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{4}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(2x-7).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=2x-7.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x-7)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-114926" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-