al in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{(2x-3)^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((2x-3)/2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2x-3}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-114906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2x-3}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2x-3}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2x-3}{4})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2x-3}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{3}^{3+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}-6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+10 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+10 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+10 \\\\  & =(x-3)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{{x}^{2}-6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{5}{(x-3)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-3.\n$$\n\n \nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $3+\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{3+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}-6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{3}^{3+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =5(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-19527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{5}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+17 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+17 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+17 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{(x-4)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{5}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-arctan\\,(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-348570" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348570" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}-4x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+5 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+5 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-4+5 \\\\  & =(x-2)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}-4x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x-2)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-2).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}-4x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-348554" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348554" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+18 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+18 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+18 \\\\  & =(x-3)^{2}+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-3)/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-3}{3}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-3}{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-6x+18}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-3)/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-114910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{9})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-3)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{3})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-3588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-8x+20}\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-3588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+20 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+20 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+20 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-8x+20}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-4)/2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-4}{2}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-4}{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-8x+20}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-4)/2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-3588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-3588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-3588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{cot}^{-1}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{cot}^{-1}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{4})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-3588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-5/2}^{-3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x-3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-4x-3 & =-({x}^{2}+4x+3) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+[{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}]+3) \\\\  & =-((x+2)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(x+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5/2}^{-3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x-3}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-5/2}^{-3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x+2.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-5/2$ | $-3/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1/2$ | $1/2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{-3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-4x-3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5/2}^{-3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-270105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{-12-x(x+12)}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12-x(x+12) & =-12-({x}^{2}+12x) \\\\  & =-12-({x}^{2}+12x+36-36) \\\\  & =-12-((x+6)^{2}-36) \\\\  & =24-(x+6)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{-12-x(x+12)}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{24-(x+6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{24(1-(x+6)^{2}/24)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{24}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+6)^{2}/(2\\sqrt{6})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+6)/2\\sqrt{6})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+6}{2\\sqrt{6}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+6}{2\\sqrt{6}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{6}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-6-\\sqrt{6}$ | $-6+\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{-12-x(x+12)}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+6)/2\\sqrt{6})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}u. \\\\  & =15{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =15(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =15(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =5\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-270103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\pi "] ["math" "5\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-270103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-2x & =-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 1x+[{1}^{2}-{1}^{2}]) \\\\  & =-((x+1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(x+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+1).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $-1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =arcsin\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-348547" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348547" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-10}^{-8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-18x-80}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-18x-80 & =-({x}^{2}+18x+80) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 9x+[{9}^{2}-{9}^{2}]+80) \\\\  & =-((x+9)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(x+9)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-10}^{-8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-18x-80}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-10}^{-8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+9)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+9).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+9.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-10$ | $-8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-10}^{-8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-18x-80}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-348550" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348550" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-238056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-13/2}^{-11/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-12x-35}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-238056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-12x-35 & =-({x}^{2}+12x+35) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 6x+[{6}^{2}-{6}^{2}]+35) \\\\  & =-((x+6)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(x+6)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-13/2}^{-11/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-12x-35}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-13/2}^{-11/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x+6.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-13/2$ | $-11/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1/2$ | $1/2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-13/2}^{-11/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-12x-35}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-13/2}^{-11/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-238056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-238056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-238056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "3\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-238056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-2+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{0}\\frac{3}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+3 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+3 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-4+3 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{0}\\frac{3}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=3{\\int }_{-2+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{0}\\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+2).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-2+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{0}\\frac{3}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2} \\\\  & =3(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}\\,(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-348530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{10}{|x-6|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-12x+35}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x+35 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+({6}^{2}-{6}^{2})+35 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-12x+36)-36+35 \\\\  & =(x-6)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{10}{|x-6|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-12x+35}}\\,\\text{d}x=10\\int \\frac{1}{|x-6|\\sqrt{(x-6)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x-6.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10}{|x-6|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-12x+35}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\int \\frac{1}{|x-6|\\sqrt{(x-6)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-6)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-19532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+6)+C"] ["math" "10\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C"] ["math" "10\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-6)+C"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{3})+C"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-3}{2})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-19532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-6)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-4+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{-2}\\frac{5}{|x+4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+8x+15 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+15 \\\\  & =(x+4)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{-2}\\frac{5}{|x+4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=5{\\int }_{-4+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{-2}\\frac{1}{|x+4|\\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-4+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{-2}\\frac{5}{|x+4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2} \\\\  & =5(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}\\,(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-348533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-348533" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+15 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-8x+16)-16+15 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x-4.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-114928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x-4}{2})+C"] ["math" "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+4)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+4}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-114928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-49689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-49689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}-25 & =25[\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}-1] \\\\  & =25[{(\\frac{x+2}{5})}^{2}-1]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{25[((x+2)/5)^{2}-1]}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\cdot \\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\cdot 5\\cdot \\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{15}{|x+2|\\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|(x+2)/5|\\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\frac{x+2}{5}.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+2}{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{75}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-25}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|(x+2)/5|\\sqrt{((x+2)/5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{5})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-49689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "847d5bd8bdb600e1c35d2fefd2641a48b1a33301d60805c08c3930557cbccc19"} {"question" "q-49689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-49689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+5}{2})+C"] ["math" "15\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{5})+C"] ["math" "15\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C"] ["math" "15\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+5)+C"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+1}{5})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "q-49689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x+2}{5})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e738b27b41d563858abb13fa6c02fcef9b568d40a9c9bf0b7bb07c141f05f4c"} {"question" "e-14577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{36 -(3x - 2)^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14577.json" "file_sha256" "914add7325e9c0ce64c1ad11dd53883e6e293d95fbb208e0de012a42312b8958"} {"question" "e-14577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36-(3x-2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36(1-(3x-2)^{2}/36)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^{2}/36}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^{2}/36}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^{2}/36}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((3x-2)/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\,\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin u + C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\left(\\dfrac{3x-2}{6}\\right).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=\\dfrac{3x-2}{6}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\textrm{d}x = 2\\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36-(3x-2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((3x-2)/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{3x-2}{6})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14577.json" "file_sha256" "914add7325e9c0ce64c1ad11dd53883e6e293d95fbb208e0de012a42312b8958"} {"question" "e-14574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2-2x + 3}\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14574.json" "file_sha256" "b70a213ffc1b4b9f822b5d8e656e29bbc8dbc71c7b2d13f84d6906175c82b3c0"} {"question" "e-14574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nx^2-2x + 3\n& = x^2 - 2 \\cdot x+ (1^2 - 1^2) + 3 \\[3pt]\n& = (x^2 - 2 \\cdot x+ 1^2) - 1 + 3 \\[3pt]\n& = (x-1)^2+2\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-1)^{2}+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{1+u^2} \\, \\textrm{d}u\n=\n\\arctan u + C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\left(\\dfrac{x-1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\dfrac{x-1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = \\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{2}})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14574.json" "file_sha256" "b70a213ffc1b4b9f822b5d8e656e29bbc8dbc71c7b2d13f84d6906175c82b3c0"} {"question" "e-14575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{4x - 4x^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14575.json" "file_sha256" "e51448b1fee4437b90df88bbf3d043341a1dc5d05d62d6804c568c98ff212351"} {"question" "e-14575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4{x}^{2} & =-(4{x}^{2}-4x) \\\\  & =-((2x)^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+1-1) \\\\  & =-((2x-1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(2x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x-4{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x-1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\,\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(2x - 1).$  \n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu =2x - 1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=2\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac12\\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x-4{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x-1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14575.json" "file_sha256" "e51448b1fee4437b90df88bbf3d043341a1dc5d05d62d6804c568c98ff212351"} {"question" "e-14576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{x^2-2x}}\\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14576.json" "file_sha256" "7a0af97bc7d6b35fe81062afcef69be0501b8f174e261786cca4ff416e3b3596"} {"question" "e-14576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n    x^2-2x&= x^2 -2x +(1-1)\\[3pt]\n              &= (x^2 -2x +1)-1\\[3pt]\n         &= (x-1)^2-1\n         \n  }\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{x^2-2x}}\\, \\textrm{d}x \n= \\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{(x-1)^2-1}}\\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^2-1}} \\, \\textrm{d}u = \\textrm{arcsec} \\, u +C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x-1.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-1.\n$$\n\n \nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=1\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $1+\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n    \\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{x^2-2x}}\\, \\textrm{d}x \n&=  \\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3}\\dfrac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{(x-1)^2-1}}\\,\\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2} \\dfrac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^2-1}}\\, \\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=  \\textrm{arcsec}\\, {u}\\Big|_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\[5pt]\n&= \\textrm{arcsec} \\left(2\\right)  - \\textrm{arcsec}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}.\n\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006356/example-14576.json" "file_sha256" "7a0af97bc7d6b35fe81062afcef69be0501b8f174e261786cca4ff416e3b3596"}] "usage" {"q-114906" [] "e-14575" [] "e-14577" [] "e-14574" [] "e-14576" [] "q-238056" []} "basis" 1116 "retractions" [[17592186068949 :question/problem "What is $∫(1)/((2x - 3)^{2} + 4)dx$?"] [17592186069094 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $∫_{-13/2}^{-11/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-x^{2} - 12x - 35}}dx$."] [17592186068430 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{36 -(3x - 2)^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068430 :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫(1)/(\\sqrt{36 - (3x - 2)^{2}})dx &= ∫(1)/(\\sqrt{36(1 - (3x - 2)^{2}/36)})dx \\\\\n&= ∫(1)/(\\sqrt{36} \\cdot \\sqrt{1 - (3x - 2)^{2}/36})dx \\\\\n&= ∫(1)/(6\\sqrt{1 - (3x - 2)^{2}/36})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}∫(1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (3x - 2)^{2}/36})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}∫(1)/(\\sqrt{1 - ((3x - 2)/6)^{2}})dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\,\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin u + C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{3x-2}{6}\\right)\n$$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\dfrac{3x-2}{6}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\textrm{d}x = 2\\,\\textrm{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u$, and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫(1)/(\\sqrt{36 - (3x - 2)^{2}})dx &= \\frac{1}{6}∫(1)/(\\sqrt{1 - ((3x - 2)/6)^{2}})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}} \\cdot 2du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\arcsin u + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\arcsin (\\frac{3x - 2}{6}) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068427 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2-2x + 3}\\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068427 :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} x^2-2x + 3 & = x^2 - 2 \\cdot x+ (1^2 - 1^2) + 3 \\\\[3pt] & = (x^2 - 2 \\cdot x+ 1^2) - 1 + 3 \\\\[3pt] & = (x-1)^2+2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{1}{x^{2} - 2x + 3}dx &= ∫(1)/((x - 1)^{2} + 2)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(1)/(1 + ((x - 1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2})dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{1+u^2} \\, \\textrm{d}u = \\arctan u + C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x-1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)\n$$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\dfrac{x-1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}x = \\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u$, and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{1}{x^{2} - 2x + 3}dx &= \\frac{1}{2}∫(1)/(1 + ((x - 1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫\\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}∫\\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\arctan u + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\arctan (\\frac{x - 1}{\\sqrt{2}}) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068428 :question/problem "Calculate ${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{4x - 4x^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186068428 :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 4x^{2} &= - (4x^{2} - 4x) \\\\\n&= - ((2x)^{2} - 2 \\cdot 2x + 1 - 1) \\\\\n&= - ((2x - 1)^{2} - 1) \\\\\n&= 1 - (2x - 1)^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x - 4x^{2}}}dx &= ∫(1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (2x - 1)^{2}})dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\,\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(2x - 1)$.\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$u =2x - 1$.\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac12\\textrm{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u$, and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x - 4x^{2}}}dx &= ∫(1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (2x - 1)^{2}})dx \\\\\n&= ∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\arcsin u + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\arcsin (2x - 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068429 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{\\mid x-1 \\mid \\sqrt{x^2-2x}}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186068429 :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} x^2-2x&= x^2 -2x +(1-1) \\\\[3pt] &= (x^2 -2x +1)-1 \\\\[3pt] &= (x-1)^2-1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{\\begin{vmatrix}x-1 & \\sqrt{x^2-2x}}\\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{\\mid x-1\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{(x-1)^2-1}}\\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\mid u \\mid \\sqrt{u^2-1}} \\, \\textrm{d}u = \\textrm{arcsec} \\, u +C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x-1$.\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n$u=x-1$.\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=1 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u$.\n\n| $x$ | $1+\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $u$ | $\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3} \\dfrac{1}{\\begin{vmatrix}x-1 & \\sqrt{x^2-2x}}\\, \\textrm{d}x &= \\int_{1+2/\\sqrt{3}}^{3}\\dfrac{1}{\\begin{vmatrix}x-1 & \\sqrt{(x-1)^2-1}}\\,\\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &=\\int_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2} \\dfrac{1}{\\mid u\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{u^2-1}}\\, \\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &= \\textrm{arcsec}\\, {u}\\Big\\end{vmatrix}_{2/\\sqrt{3}}^{2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\textrm{arcsec} \\left(2\\right) - \\textrm{arcsec}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}. \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186065489 17592186065490 17592186065491 17592186065492 17592186065493 17592186066155 17592186066156 17592186066157 17592186066158 17592186066159] "immutable_fields" [[17592186065488 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065488 :answer-field/id] [17592186065488 :answer-field/key] [17592186065488 :answer-field/type] [17592186066154 :answer-field/correct] [17592186066154 :answer-field/id] [17592186066154 :answer-field/key] [17592186066154 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
